__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.venv/
*.egg
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.png
*.html
*.svg
# EXAMPLES.md/README.md embed these two as <img> -- keep them trackable so
# the images aren't broken links on GitHub.
!assets/svg-examples/*.svg
# Vendored relief/elevation rasters make_choropleth.py and
# make_situation_map.py load at render time (relief-lowres.png,
# elevation-30arcsec.png) -- data assets, not generated output; without
# this exception the blanket *.png rule above silently drops them and a
# fresh clone's relief layer breaks with no error, just a missing file.
!assets/geo/*.png
# doc/CARTOGRAPHY.tex's own figures (print resolution, regenerable via the
# scripts/build_*_figures.py trio, but the .tex \includegraphics calls need
# them present to compile without running those scripts first).
!doc/img/*.png

.private/
# Coverage reports
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml

.DS_Store


demo-data/

!assets/logo.png

# doc/CARTOGRAPHY.tex compiles locally with xelatex/biber (see that file's
# own header). doc/CARTOGRAPHY.pdf is the one meant to ship in the repo for
# readers without a LaTeX toolchain, so it stays tracked (via Git LFS, see
# .gitattributes) despite the *.html rule above having no equivalent
# blanket rule to except it from. Everything else here is disposable
# build-tool output, regenerated on every compile.
*.docx
*.aux
*.bbl
*.bcf
*.blg
*.fdb_latexmk
*.fls
*.log
*.out
*.run.xml
*.synctex.gz
*.toc
